WEBVTT

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.126
You're late.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.127
Sorry, sir.

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:32.562
What's the threshold
of the H2 molecule?

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.657
14.7 electron volts.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:35.928
Third brightest star in Orion?

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:37.094
Viewed from where?

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.398
Earth.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:40.063
Gamma Orionis

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.665
or Bellatrix if you prefer
the original Arabic name.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:43.709
Not bad.

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:45.836
Now, give me a hug, Katie.

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:47.174
That's an order.

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:49.807
I wasn't expecting a pop quiz.

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:51.510
Just wanted to make
sure all those pips

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:53.711
haven't made you forget
you're a scientist first.

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:55.152
How could they?

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.712
I still have nightmares about
your fractal calculus final.

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.826
There's still some work
to be done,

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:04.261
but once the sawdust clears,
I think you'll be impressed.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.697
Voyager may not be
as big as a Galaxy-class ship,

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:10.930
but she's quick and smart...
like her Captain.

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:14.667
700,000 metric tons,
15 decks, computer systems

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:17.209
augmented
with bio-neural circuitry.

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:18.938
Top cruising speed...
warp 9.975.

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:20.309
Deck 1.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.404
Of course, I expect

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.449
to get that up
another notch or two.

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:25.950
Sounds like you already know
your ship pretty well.

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:27.849
I've been buried
in Voyager's schematics

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:29.081
for the past three months.

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:31.623
I could walk the corridors
blindfolded.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:35.286
You might not want
to shut your eyes just yet.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:38.159
Captain on the Bridge.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:40.324
As you were.

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:44.964
It's bigger than I expected.

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:48.496
Schematics never fully prepare
you for the real thing.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.839
Try it on.

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:04.813
Don't get too comfortable.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:07.325
I have more to show you.

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:19.137
Your home away from home.

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:20.263
Coffee?

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.433
Oh, no, thanks.

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:24.534
Coffee. Black.

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:29.508
Any word from Tuvok?

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.345
Not yet.

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:33.317
Shouldn't he have
made contact by now?

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:35.251
We know he's aboard
Chakotay's ship.

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:36.583
He's probably decided

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:38.385
not to risk exposure
until he has to.

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:40.426
Catching up with him
in the Badlands

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:41.755
is going to be tricky,

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:44.262
even in a ship as quick
and smart as Voyager.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:47.356
I've heard about a pilot
who might make the job easier.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.526
Who's that?

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.593
Tom Paris.

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:53.696
Admiral Paris's son?

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:55.297
Correct me

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:57.468
if I'm wrong, but he's
serving a sentence for...

00:02:57.544 --> 00:02:59.341
He's made some mistakes.

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:04.308
But everybody deserves
a second chance.

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:07.409
I'll look into it.

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:11.587
If it's not too late,

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:14.024
I'd like to recalibrate
the navigational sensors.

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:15.617
I think I can enhance the range.

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:18.721
Your coffee's not even cold,
you're already making changes.

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:20.060
Excuse us, Ensign.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:22.533
I like a ship that knows
where it's going.

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:25.799
I assure you, Voyager has
the best sensors in the fleet.

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:27.965
There's always room
for improvement.

00:05:29.329 --> 00:05:30.261
The Bridge is clear.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:31.592
There's no sign of the weapon.

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:32.790
Continue scanning.

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:34.196
Acknowledged.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.462
Your briefing room.

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:40.938
Starfleet's

00:05:41.074 --> 00:05:43.372
most up-to-date vessel
and they still can't design

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:45.536
a comfortable place
to hold a meeting.

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:46.942
What do you think, Ensign?

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.707
Captain?

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:51.147
What's your opinion
of this room?

00:05:53.086 --> 00:05:55.111
It is an efficient design.

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:57.918
Well, there you have it,
Admiral.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.218
It's efficient.

00:05:59.292 --> 00:06:00.657
I must be wrong.

00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:01.887
Carry on.

00:06:12.672 --> 00:06:14.105
We've added a new system

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:16.903
we're thinking of installing
throughout the fleet.

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:18.568
The Emergency Medical Hologram.

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:19.872
I'm up-to-date.

00:06:19.946 --> 00:06:21.208
Computer, activate EMH.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:23.646
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:24.808
It's programmed

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:26.818
with over four million
surgical procedures.

00:06:26.886 --> 00:06:29.150
Five million
and the medical knowledge

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:30.655
of over 3,000 cultures.

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:32.156
Impressive.

00:06:32.225 --> 00:06:33.522
Did you call me to chitchat

00:06:33.593 --> 00:06:35.185
or is there an actual emergency?

00:06:35.261 --> 00:06:36.922
His personality
could use some work.

00:06:36.996 --> 00:06:38.088
I'm designed to practice

00:06:38.164 --> 00:06:40.064
medicine
as efficiently as possible.

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:42.601
Small talk only compromises
my performance.

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:43.657
Thank you, Doctor.

00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:45.363
Computer, deactivate EMH.

00:06:49.342 --> 00:06:50.639
Thank you.

00:07:01.521 --> 00:07:03.079
Hello.

00:07:03.156 --> 00:07:04.180
Sir.

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:05.986
Lieutenant Carey.

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:08.458
I don't think we've met.

00:07:08.528 --> 00:07:09.825
Jameson, Anna.

00:07:09.896 --> 00:07:11.887
Service number 860790.

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:13.226
I'm not security.

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:15.733
I'm just... trying
to get to know

00:07:15.802 --> 00:07:17.997
all the new faces around here.

00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:21.305
What are you working on?

00:07:21.374 --> 00:07:25.071
I am attempting to realign
the EPS manifolds.

00:07:25.144 --> 00:07:26.805
Do you need a hand?

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:28.073
No.

00:07:28.147 --> 00:07:30.308
Well, maybe I'll see you
in the Mess Hall later.

00:07:30.383 --> 00:07:31.315
Unlikely.

00:07:31.384 --> 00:07:32.510
Hmm?

00:07:32.585 --> 00:07:34.553
I am not a member
of Voyager's crew.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:36.918
I'm on assignment here
at Utopia Planitia.

00:07:37.056 --> 00:07:38.148
Too bad.

00:07:38.224 --> 00:07:41.159
Well... next time
I'm in the neighborhood,

00:07:41.227 --> 00:07:43.195
I'll drop by and say hello.

00:08:00.813 --> 00:08:02.644
I wish Starfleet would give me
more than three weeks.

00:08:02.715 --> 00:08:03.682
With a little more time,

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:05.341
we could really
explore the Badlands.

00:08:05.418 --> 00:08:06.680
You haven't changed a bit.

00:08:08.387 --> 00:08:09.786
Main Engineering.

00:08:09.856 --> 00:08:14.259
Class-9 warp drive,
tricyclic input manifold.

00:08:16.195 --> 00:08:19.426
You'll be the first to test it
in deep space.

00:08:33.546 --> 00:08:36.879
I've localized
the temporal distortions...

00:08:36.949 --> 00:08:38.849
Deck 4, Section 39.

00:09:04.777 --> 00:09:06.108
I've found the weapon.

00:09:06.178 --> 00:09:07.668
Begin the procedure.

00:09:19.592 --> 00:09:22.060
Problem?

00:09:22.128 --> 00:09:24.892
One of the EPS relays
just went off-line.

00:09:25.031 --> 00:09:26.896
Voyager's first malfunction.

00:09:27.033 --> 00:09:28.227
I'm sorry, Captain.

00:09:28.301 --> 00:09:30.633
I tested those systems
this morning.

00:09:30.703 --> 00:09:32.102
As you were, Lieutenant.

00:09:32.171 --> 00:09:34.469
I've been looking forward
to getting my hands dirty.

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:36.337
Hmm.

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:46.279
The weapon is out of phase.

00:09:46.352 --> 00:09:48.820
You've sent me
to the wrong time frame.

00:09:48.888 --> 00:09:51.516
At least we know
where the weapon was placed.

00:09:51.591 --> 00:09:53.252
Now we have to determine when.

00:09:57.229 --> 00:09:59.288
This hatch is locked
from the inside.

00:09:59.365 --> 00:10:00.696
This isn't a secure area.

00:10:00.766 --> 00:10:02.734
None of these hatches
should be sealed.

00:10:02.802 --> 00:10:05.396
I'm reading some kind
of chroniton flux.

00:10:05.471 --> 00:10:06.904
Chronitons?

00:10:06.973 --> 00:10:09.703
It's coming from inside
this Jefferies tube.

00:10:09.775 --> 00:10:12.903
Patterson to Security.
Seal off Deck 4.

00:10:15.648 --> 00:10:17.343
I've been detected.
I must leave.

00:10:17.416 --> 00:10:19.577
There's too much interference
from the weapon.

00:10:19.652 --> 00:10:21.677
Recalibrate
your temporal transport beacon.

00:10:21.754 --> 00:10:23.085
Understood.

00:10:23.155 --> 00:10:25.715
We can access Section 39
through here.

00:10:31.397 --> 00:10:34.264
Scramble the locking mechanism
before they get in.

00:10:34.333 --> 00:10:36.563
Hurry. They're approaching
your coordinates.

00:10:36.636 --> 00:10:38.729
You'll need to reset
the command controls.

00:10:38.804 --> 00:10:41.466
Stand by. We're trying
to get you out of there.

00:10:59.025 --> 00:10:59.957
It's time.

00:11:00.026 --> 00:11:00.993
Pull her out.

00:11:01.127 --> 00:11:02.526
There's too much interference.

00:11:02.595 --> 00:11:03.584
If I transport her now,

00:11:03.663 --> 00:11:05.187
we'll damage
her bionetic implants.

00:11:05.264 --> 00:11:06.925
If we don't, Captain
Janeway's going to find her.

00:11:07.066 --> 00:11:08.124
It'll contaminate the timeline.

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:09.531
- Sir...
- Now.

00:11:11.737 --> 00:11:14.365
Temporal transport in progress.

00:11:29.588 --> 00:11:31.385
Question, Admiral.

00:11:31.457 --> 00:11:35.188
What causes
a chroniton flux of.003?

00:11:35.261 --> 00:11:37.456
I don't know.

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:42.695
Neither do I, but whoever
or whatever it was...

00:11:42.768 --> 00:11:45.498
it's gone now.

00:11:48.574 --> 00:11:51.907
The subject is approaching
the temporal threshold.

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:10.324
I told you
this was going to happen.

00:12:10.396 --> 00:12:11.693
She's dead.

00:12:27.346 --> 00:12:28.904
Any luck reviving her?

00:12:28.981 --> 00:12:29.948
No, sir.

00:12:30.015 --> 00:12:31.414
We'll have to recruit her again.

00:12:31.484 --> 00:12:33.952
Sir, a fourth jump,
she could suffer neural damage...

00:12:34.053 --> 00:12:35.418
even temporal psychosis.

00:12:35.488 --> 00:12:37.786
Unless we repair the timeline,
she's going to die.

00:12:37.857 --> 00:12:40.792
We're giving her another chance
to save her crew and herself.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.691
We'll go back
and retrieve Seven of Nine

00:12:42.762 --> 00:12:44.354
a microsecond
before the explosion.

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:46.455
That way no one will
notice she's gone.

00:12:46.532 --> 00:12:48.830
Tempus fugit, Lieutenant.

00:12:48.901 --> 00:12:51.165
Raise shields.

00:12:51.237 --> 00:12:57.506
Time frame... Stardate 52861.274.
Delta Quadrant.

00:12:57.576 --> 00:13:02.673
Spatial coordinates...
87-Theta by 271.

00:13:02.748 --> 00:13:06.377
Target... USS Voyager.

00:13:10.623 --> 00:13:12.614
Follow the light

00:13:12.691 --> 00:13:14.921
to the left,

00:13:14.994 --> 00:13:17.121
right,

00:13:17.196 --> 00:13:19.790
and up,

00:13:19.865 --> 00:13:21.196
and down.

00:13:23.636 --> 00:13:25.661
Hmm.

00:13:28.741 --> 00:13:31.539
I ran
a complete self-diagnostic.

00:13:31.610 --> 00:13:33.271
Mm-hmm?

00:13:33.345 --> 00:13:35.438
At first, I thought
my ocular implants

00:13:35.514 --> 00:13:36.606
were malfunctioning.

00:13:36.682 --> 00:13:39.708
However, after consulting
the Starfleet medical database,

00:13:39.785 --> 00:13:42.253
I realize it's a flaw
in my human physiology.

00:13:42.321 --> 00:13:44.789
Specifically?

00:13:44.857 --> 00:13:46.552
I'm experiencing
dizziness, double vision.

00:13:46.625 --> 00:13:47.614
After considering

00:13:47.693 --> 00:13:49.558
all potential environmental
and genetic factors,

00:13:49.628 --> 00:13:51.323
I've concluded
that I am suffering

00:13:51.397 --> 00:13:52.955
from Albright-Salzman syndrome.

00:13:53.098 --> 00:13:54.963
A rare neurological condition

00:13:55.034 --> 00:13:57.662
that hasn't affected
a single human being

00:13:57.736 --> 00:13:58.896
for over two centuries.

00:13:58.971 --> 00:14:00.598
Unlikely.

00:14:00.673 --> 00:14:02.607
Human physiology is imperfect...

00:14:02.675 --> 00:14:05.041
susceptible
to a variety of disorders.

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:06.737
True, but in this instance,

00:14:06.812 --> 00:14:08.643
we can safely say
you're suffering

00:14:08.714 --> 00:14:10.773
from a mild case
of sensory aphasia...

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:13.717
a minor disruption
to your neuro-receptors.

00:14:13.786 --> 00:14:15.549
Neither rare,
nor life-threatening.

00:14:15.621 --> 00:14:19.079
Apparently I was in need
of a second opinion.

00:14:19.158 --> 00:14:21.558
That's the danger
of self-diagnosis...

00:14:21.627 --> 00:14:23.754
patients always
assume the worst.

00:14:23.829 --> 00:14:25.387
This should clear it up.

00:14:31.503 --> 00:14:33.164
How do things look now?

00:14:33.239 --> 00:14:34.729
Normal.

00:14:34.807 --> 00:14:37.105
Doctor,
please report to Sick Bay.

00:14:37.176 --> 00:14:38.268
On my way.

00:14:38.344 --> 00:14:40.642
Next time your human
physiology fails you,

00:14:40.713 --> 00:14:41.941
don't consult the database.

00:14:42.014 --> 00:14:43.777
Just call me.

00:14:43.849 --> 00:14:45.942
You are the database.

00:14:46.051 --> 00:14:49.248
With two legs
and a splendid bedside manner.

00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:00.159
A curious exercise.

00:15:00.232 --> 00:15:01.893
Yeah, Ping-Pong.

00:15:01.967 --> 00:15:03.093
You should try it.

00:15:03.168 --> 00:15:05.830
It's a great test
of hand-eye coordination.

00:15:05.905 --> 00:15:07.395
I don't require testing.

00:15:07.473 --> 00:15:12.467
Yeah, so the Doc tells me...
a visual acuity index of 99.6.

00:15:13.979 --> 00:15:16.345
You know, you'd be
great at this game.

00:15:16.415 --> 00:15:17.507
Why don't you be my partner

00:15:17.583 --> 00:15:19.050
in the doubles
tournament tonight?

00:15:19.118 --> 00:15:20.449
Chapman was supposed to play,

00:15:20.519 --> 00:15:22.919
but he's come down with
a nasty case of space sickness.

00:15:23.022 --> 00:15:24.216
I'm busy.

00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:25.416
Oh.

00:15:25.491 --> 00:15:26.617
Too bad.

00:15:26.692 --> 00:15:28.421
Well, I guess I'll have
to tell B'Elanna

00:15:28.494 --> 00:15:30.189
that you thought
you couldn't beat her.

00:15:30.262 --> 00:15:32.753
You're attempting
to appeal to my vanity.

00:15:32.831 --> 00:15:34.560
Is it working?

00:15:34.633 --> 00:15:36.794
I will consider your request.

00:15:36.869 --> 00:15:39.770
It's yes or no, Seven...
the tournament's tonight.

00:15:42.608 --> 00:15:43.597
Yes.

00:15:43.676 --> 00:15:44.700
Great.

00:15:44.777 --> 00:15:46.677
Meet me in the Mess Hall
at 1900 hours.

00:15:46.745 --> 00:15:48.975
We'll get in a little practice
first.

00:15:54.753 --> 00:15:57.187
Captain, you don't look well.

00:15:57.256 --> 00:15:58.655
Come in, please.

00:15:58.724 --> 00:15:59.952
I'm sure it's nothing serious.

00:16:00.092 --> 00:16:01.218
Symptoms?

00:16:01.293 --> 00:16:03.386
Nausea, dizziness.

00:16:03.462 --> 00:16:05.760
It looks like a simple case
of space sickness...

00:16:05.831 --> 00:16:07.389
the third one
I've treated today.

00:16:07.466 --> 00:16:09.991
That's odd. We haven't
run into any turbulence.

00:16:10.069 --> 00:16:11.730
It's possible
the inertial dampers

00:16:11.804 --> 00:16:12.862
are out of alignment.

00:16:12.938 --> 00:16:14.735
Even so, I've been
on some pretty rough rides.

00:16:14.807 --> 00:16:16.741
It's never affected me
like this.

00:16:16.809 --> 00:16:18.299
It happens to everyone.

00:16:18.377 --> 00:16:22.370
20 milligrams of inaprovaline
should restore your space legs.

00:16:22.448 --> 00:16:23.540
I'll check the dampers.

00:16:23.615 --> 00:16:25.139
Double-check your bio-readings.

00:16:25.217 --> 00:16:27.208
See if there's
another explanation.

00:16:39.665 --> 00:16:40.927
Point, server.

00:16:41.033 --> 00:16:43.297
It's all in the wrist.

00:16:43.369 --> 00:16:44.768
Score?

00:16:44.837 --> 00:16:46.737
19-18.

00:16:56.782 --> 00:16:59.114
Say good night, Harry.

00:17:03.555 --> 00:17:05.580
What do you call that shot?

00:17:07.393 --> 00:17:09.588
I'm reading
temporal distortions.

00:17:28.647 --> 00:17:29.579
Report.

00:17:29.648 --> 00:17:30.740
The temporal distortions

00:17:30.816 --> 00:17:32.750
are fracturing space-time
throughout the ship.

00:17:32.818 --> 00:17:33.750
Cause?

00:17:33.819 --> 00:17:34.808
Unknown.

00:17:34.887 --> 00:17:37.253
They appear to be emanating
from Deck 4, Section 39.

00:17:37.322 --> 00:17:38.812
We've already
erected force fields,

00:17:38.891 --> 00:17:40.449
but they're not
having much effect.

00:17:40.526 --> 00:17:42.426
If we can't find
a way to stop them,

00:17:42.494 --> 00:17:43.927
they'll tear the ship apart.

00:17:44.063 --> 00:17:45.496
How much time do we have?

00:17:45.564 --> 00:17:46.826
Two hours, at most.

00:17:46.899 --> 00:17:49.094
Go to Deck 4 and find out
what we're dealing with.

00:17:49.168 --> 00:17:51.830
Let's see if we can find a way
to enhance the force fields.

00:17:56.642 --> 00:18:00.169
An injection a day keeps
space sickness away.

00:18:00.245 --> 00:18:03.612
You try to be funny after
treating 37 cases of nausea.

00:18:03.682 --> 00:18:04.671
Janeway to Sick Bay.

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:05.876
Go ahead.

00:18:06.018 --> 00:18:07.645
We've found the source
of our epidemic...

00:18:07.719 --> 00:18:09.050
temporal distortions.

00:18:09.121 --> 00:18:11.112
I was beginning to suspect
some kind of anomaly.

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:12.418
I've designed a treatment

00:18:12.491 --> 00:18:14.186
that seems to be inhibiting
the symptoms.

00:18:14.259 --> 00:18:15.191
Keep me posted.

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:16.192
Aye, Captain.

00:18:16.261 --> 00:18:17.489
Neelix to the Doctor.

00:18:17.563 --> 00:18:19.827
I've got a medical emergency
in the Mess Hall.

00:18:19.898 --> 00:18:21.456
Ensign Mannus is violently ill.

00:18:21.533 --> 00:18:22.625
On my way.

00:18:22.701 --> 00:18:23.861
Take over here.

00:18:28.740 --> 00:18:31.072
Doctor, shall I whip you
up a photonic snack?

00:18:31.143 --> 00:18:32.508
Where's the medical emergency?

00:18:32.578 --> 00:18:34.478
I hope you're not referring
to this pot roast.

00:18:34.546 --> 00:18:35.877
You called me a few minutes ago.

00:18:35.948 --> 00:18:37.279
You said Ensign Mannus was ill.

00:18:37.349 --> 00:18:38.281
I did?

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:39.317
Yes.

00:18:39.384 --> 00:18:40.817
Ensign Mannus is
right over there.

00:18:40.886 --> 00:18:42.217
He came in an hour ago.

00:18:42.287 --> 00:18:44.187
He looks perfectly norm...

00:18:51.964 --> 00:18:53.431
Acute space sickness.

00:18:53.499 --> 00:18:55.194
Good thing you were here.

00:18:55.267 --> 00:18:57.827
I wouldn't have been,
if you hadn't...

00:18:57.903 --> 00:18:59.871
Temporal distortions.

00:18:59.938 --> 00:19:00.927
Doctor?

00:19:01.039 --> 00:19:04.531
This is all starting
to make sense.

00:19:04.610 --> 00:19:08.603
In Sick Bay, it's
1500 hours, 43 minutes,

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:12.673
but in the Mess Hall, it's 1536.

00:19:12.751 --> 00:19:14.981
Seven minutes earlier.

00:19:15.053 --> 00:19:16.486
I did get a call from you.

00:19:16.555 --> 00:19:18.284
You just haven't made it yet.

00:19:21.660 --> 00:19:23.423
Coffee, black.

00:19:26.298 --> 00:19:27.697
Come in.

00:19:27.766 --> 00:19:29.734
Before you say anything,

00:19:29.801 --> 00:19:31.894
let me remind you what happens
to bearers of bad news.

00:19:32.037 --> 00:19:33.595
Don't kill the messenger.

00:19:33.672 --> 00:19:34.798
Go ahead, fire.

00:19:34.873 --> 00:19:37.000
It looks like these space-time
fractures are growing stronger.

00:19:37.075 --> 00:19:39.202
We're detecting temporal
paradoxes throughout the ship.

00:19:39.278 --> 00:19:40.472
Paradoxes?

00:19:40.546 --> 00:19:42.844
Internal chronometers show

00:19:42.915 --> 00:19:46.282
it's 0600 on Deck 9
and 0605 on Deck 13.

00:19:46.351 --> 00:19:49.013
Time's passing more quickly
in some parts of the ship

00:19:49.087 --> 00:19:50.452
and slowing down in others.

00:19:50.522 --> 00:19:52.251
Maybe that explains
why this coffee

00:19:52.324 --> 00:19:53.916
tastes like it's three days old.

00:19:54.026 --> 00:19:56.051
The same thing's been
happening in the Mess Hall.

00:19:56.128 --> 00:19:58.562
Food replicated less than an
hour ago is already spoiled.

00:19:58.630 --> 00:19:59.654
I've been working

00:19:59.731 --> 00:20:01.460
on a way to enhance
our containment fields

00:20:01.533 --> 00:20:03.023
to keep the fractures
from spreading.

00:20:03.101 --> 00:20:05.865
I'll get a team on it
right away.

00:20:05.938 --> 00:20:07.166
In the meantime,
we should evacuate

00:20:07.239 --> 00:20:08.831
the affected areas.

00:20:08.907 --> 00:20:09.839
See to it.

00:20:09.908 --> 00:20:11.603
There's one other problem.

00:20:11.677 --> 00:20:13.076
Turbolifts... Turbolifts...
Turbolifts 2 and 3...

00:20:13.145 --> 00:20:14.544
2 and 3 are off-line...
are off-line... so we've

00:20:14.613 --> 00:20:16.308
been using... so we've been
using... the Jefferies tube.

00:20:16.381 --> 00:20:17.973
...using the Jefferies tube.

00:20:24.690 --> 00:20:26.089
Captain?

00:20:26.158 --> 00:20:28.524
There's a temporal distortion
intersecting this room.

00:20:28.594 --> 00:20:29.686
It's expanding.

00:20:29.761 --> 00:20:31.820
Time to test
your new containment fields.

00:20:35.234 --> 00:20:37.327
This is where
they're coming from.

00:20:37.402 --> 00:20:40.633
I still can't tell
what's causing them.

00:20:47.613 --> 00:20:49.376
What is it?

00:20:49.448 --> 00:20:51.143
A piece of technology.

00:20:51.216 --> 00:20:53.684
It's emitting
temporal distortions.

00:20:53.752 --> 00:20:55.686
Why can't I see it?

00:20:55.754 --> 00:21:00.248
My ocular implant can detect
irregularities in space-time.

00:21:00.325 --> 00:21:01.622
Torres to Bridge.

00:21:01.693 --> 00:21:03.183
We've found the problem.

00:21:03.262 --> 00:21:06.288
There's some kind of device
in Junction Beta-28.

00:21:06.365 --> 00:21:07.730
Beam it off the ship.

00:21:07.799 --> 00:21:10.393
I can't get a lock.

00:21:10.469 --> 00:21:14.371
The distortions are beginning
to demolecularize the hull.

00:21:15.774 --> 00:21:17.298
Hull breach...
Ventral Section 14.

00:21:25.717 --> 00:21:27.912
Captain, I'm picking up
a strange reading on Deck 4.

00:21:27.986 --> 00:21:29.476
What kind of reading?

00:21:29.554 --> 00:21:30.885
It's a chroniton flux... .003.

00:21:30.956 --> 00:21:32.856
More distortions?

00:21:32.924 --> 00:21:34.687
I don't think so.

00:21:38.797 --> 00:21:40.128
Dry dock.

00:21:40.198 --> 00:21:41.893
Ma'am?

00:21:41.967 --> 00:21:43.958
The first time
I saw these readings was...

00:21:44.036 --> 00:21:45.731
five years ago?

00:21:45.804 --> 00:21:47.499
Voyager was still in dry dock.

00:21:47.572 --> 00:21:49.233
Same readings, same location.

00:21:49.308 --> 00:21:50.570
What caused them?

00:21:50.642 --> 00:21:53.440
I never found out.

00:21:55.681 --> 00:21:57.546
We're losing
structural integrity.

00:21:57.616 --> 00:21:59.516
Multiple breaches... all decks.

00:21:59.584 --> 00:22:01.518
Emergency systems are failing.

00:22:01.586 --> 00:22:04.054
The distortions
are ripping us apart.

00:22:04.122 --> 00:22:05.919
We have to abandon ship.

00:22:08.493 --> 00:22:10.688
All hands, this is the Captain.

00:22:10.762 --> 00:22:13.458
Proceed to the escape pods
and abandon ship.

00:22:13.532 --> 00:22:16.023
Repeat: Abandon ship.

00:22:16.101 --> 00:22:19.502
Program the pods for a heading
of 178 mark 4.

00:22:19.571 --> 00:22:21.937
We'll rendezvous in orbit
of an M-Class planet

00:22:22.040 --> 00:22:23.439
at those coordinates.

00:22:23.508 --> 00:22:25.772
Repeat: All hands,

00:22:25.844 --> 00:22:28.312
proceed to the escape pods
and abandon ship.

00:22:33.785 --> 00:22:35.480
Identify yourselves.

00:22:35.554 --> 00:22:36.919
No time.

00:23:06.718 --> 00:23:07.878
Welcome back.

00:23:07.953 --> 00:23:09.580
Why have you brought me here?

00:23:09.654 --> 00:23:12.384
For some reason, I always
think you'll remember.

00:23:12.457 --> 00:23:13.549
I'm Captain Braxton.

00:23:13.625 --> 00:23:15.092
This is Lieutenant Ducane.

00:23:15.160 --> 00:23:18.561
You're aboard the Federation
Timeship Relativity.

00:23:18.630 --> 00:23:20.655
I'm no longer
in the 24th century.

00:23:20.732 --> 00:23:21.858
No.

00:23:21.933 --> 00:23:23.924
For you, it's almost
500 years later.

00:23:24.069 --> 00:23:26.299
We've brought you here
to help us solve a mystery.

00:23:26.371 --> 00:23:27.633
Someone... we don't know who...

00:23:27.706 --> 00:23:29.799
has planted a weapon
aboard Voyager.

00:23:29.875 --> 00:23:31.934
It's designed
to fracture space-time

00:23:32.077 --> 00:23:34.307
within a radius of 150 meters.

00:23:34.379 --> 00:23:35.778
Why do you need me?

00:23:35.847 --> 00:23:37.109
Your ocular implant.

00:23:37.182 --> 00:23:39.377
It can detect disruptions
in space-time

00:23:39.451 --> 00:23:40.816
better than our sensors.

00:23:40.886 --> 00:23:43.514
You're more familiar
with Voyager and her crew,

00:23:43.588 --> 00:23:46.216
less likely to arouse suspicion.

00:23:48.260 --> 00:23:50.353
So far, you've been
quite useful.

00:23:50.429 --> 00:23:51.555
So far?

00:23:51.630 --> 00:23:54.497
We've recruited you twice
before for this mission.

00:23:54.566 --> 00:23:55.590
Take a look.

00:24:00.205 --> 00:24:01.968
A force-3 temporal disrupter.

00:24:02.040 --> 00:24:03.405
Your previous attempts

00:24:03.475 --> 00:24:04.999
to disable it have
been unsuccessful.

00:24:05.076 --> 00:24:06.839
We're trying
to catch the saboteur

00:24:06.912 --> 00:24:09.142
before he places the weapon
on Voyager.

00:24:09.214 --> 00:24:10.476
Do you have a suspect?

00:24:10.549 --> 00:24:11.607
Not yet.

00:24:11.683 --> 00:24:13.913
Do you know
when the device was placed?

00:24:13.985 --> 00:24:17.512
Not precisely, but we've
narrowed the window to a period

00:24:17.589 --> 00:24:19.614
two years
before you joined the crew

00:24:19.691 --> 00:24:22.091
when the ship was under attack.

00:24:22.160 --> 00:24:23.923
Species 329... the Kazon.

00:24:24.062 --> 00:24:25.529
Our database indicates
that Voyager

00:24:25.597 --> 00:24:27.326
was boarded twice
during that period.

00:24:27.399 --> 00:24:28.923
The Kazon are
an inferior species.

00:24:29.067 --> 00:24:31.092
They don't possess
the technology to create

00:24:31.169 --> 00:24:32.227
such a complex weapon.

00:24:32.304 --> 00:24:34.602
We believe the saboteur
infiltrated this time frame

00:24:34.673 --> 00:24:36.231
because Voyager's shields
were down.

00:24:36.308 --> 00:24:40.404
It was the perfect opportunity
to evade detection.

00:24:40.479 --> 00:24:42.572
If I fail,
you will recruit me again.

00:24:42.647 --> 00:24:44.672
If necessary.

00:24:44.749 --> 00:24:46.376
But this will be the third time

00:24:46.451 --> 00:24:48.942
you're going to be removed
from your time frame.

00:24:49.087 --> 00:24:51.681
If we do it a fourth,
there could be certain...

00:24:51.756 --> 00:24:52.780
side effects.

00:24:52.858 --> 00:24:53.790
Side effects.

00:24:53.859 --> 00:24:56.760
You might experience
sensory aphasia.

00:24:56.828 --> 00:24:58.557
It affects the cerebral cortex

00:24:58.630 --> 00:25:00.860
and can lead
to temporal psychosis.

00:25:00.932 --> 00:25:04.060
But in your case, we're hoping
third time's a charm, eh?

00:25:04.135 --> 00:25:05.432
I'll do my best.

00:25:05.504 --> 00:25:07.301
Bring her up to date
on our protocols.

00:25:07.372 --> 00:25:09.101
Aye, sir.

00:25:09.174 --> 00:25:12.200
When you're finished here,
meet me in Holo-Matrix 1.

00:25:12.277 --> 00:25:13.801
I've prepared a simulation.

00:25:19.451 --> 00:25:21.419
Let's see how much
you've assimilated.

00:25:21.486 --> 00:25:22.783
The Dali Paradox?

00:25:22.854 --> 00:25:24.685
Also known
as the melting clock effect.

00:25:24.756 --> 00:25:26.485
It refers to a temporal fissure

00:25:26.558 --> 00:25:29.322
which slows the passage
of time to a gradual halt.

00:25:29.394 --> 00:25:30.554
The Pogo Paradox?

00:25:30.629 --> 00:25:31.857
A causality loop

00:25:31.930 --> 00:25:33.921
in which interference
to prevent an event

00:25:34.032 --> 00:25:35.693
actually triggers
the same event.

00:25:35.767 --> 00:25:36.734
Excellent.

00:25:36.801 --> 00:25:38.359
Can you give me an example?

00:25:38.436 --> 00:25:40.404
The Borg once
traveled back in time

00:25:40.472 --> 00:25:43.373
to stop Zephram Cochrane
from breaking the warp barrier.

00:25:43.441 --> 00:25:45.136
They succeeded, but that,
in turn

00:25:45.210 --> 00:25:47.508
led the Starship Enterprise
to intervene.

00:25:47.579 --> 00:25:48.944
They assisted Cochrane

00:25:49.014 --> 00:25:51.346
with the flight the Borg
were trying to prevent.

00:25:51.416 --> 00:25:52.747
Causal loop complete.

00:25:52.817 --> 00:25:55.911
So, in a way, the Federation
owes its existence to the Borg?

00:25:55.987 --> 00:25:57.352
You're welcome.

00:25:57.422 --> 00:25:59.322
The Seven of Nine Paradox.

00:25:59.391 --> 00:26:00.858
I beg your pardon?

00:26:00.926 --> 00:26:03.292
How we do know that
my presence on Voyager

00:26:03.361 --> 00:26:04.885
will not alter the timeline?

00:26:05.030 --> 00:26:07.430
You know, you've asked
me this every time?

00:26:07.499 --> 00:26:08.898
What's been your response?

00:26:09.034 --> 00:26:11.594
That uncertainty is
part of the equation.

00:26:11.670 --> 00:26:14.298
We don't know
what's going to happen.

00:26:14.372 --> 00:26:16.567
I don't enjoy uncertainty.

00:26:16.641 --> 00:26:20.475
Neither do I, but I trust
Captain Braxton's instincts

00:26:20.545 --> 00:26:23.844
just as you trust
Captain Janeway's.

00:26:23.915 --> 00:26:25.382
This is a simulation

00:26:25.450 --> 00:26:27.680
of Junction 49
on Voyager's fourth deck.

00:26:27.752 --> 00:26:30.721
Thanks to you, we've learned
that the temporal disrupter

00:26:30.789 --> 00:26:32.484
was, and will be,
concealed here.

00:26:32.557 --> 00:26:36.357
I gave up trying to keep my
tenses straight years ago.

00:26:36.428 --> 00:26:37.918
How will I disarm it?

00:26:37.996 --> 00:26:40.396
You've already tried...
unsuccessfully.

00:26:40.465 --> 00:26:42.433
The weapon's out of phase.

00:26:42.500 --> 00:26:45.731
You'll have to find the saboteur
before he plants it.

00:26:45.804 --> 00:26:47.931
This will detect
any chroniton flux

00:26:48.006 --> 00:26:50.736
other than your own,
and I'm authorizing you

00:26:50.809 --> 00:26:53.243
to use whatever force
may be necessary.

00:26:53.311 --> 00:26:55.506
Understood.

00:26:55.580 --> 00:26:58.378
One more thing... watch
out for the Janeway factor.

00:26:58.450 --> 00:27:01.044
I am not familiar
with that protocol.

00:27:01.119 --> 00:27:03.644
Your Captain has a knack
for sticking her nose

00:27:03.722 --> 00:27:04.984
where it doesn't belong,

00:27:05.056 --> 00:27:07.251
especially when it
comes to time travel.

00:27:07.325 --> 00:27:09.350
Captain Janeway is
quite resourceful.

00:27:09.427 --> 00:27:12.089
Has it occurred to you
that she may be helpful?

00:27:12.163 --> 00:27:14.222
Helpful? That woman
has been responsible

00:27:14.299 --> 00:27:15.891
for three major
temporal incursions.

00:27:15.967 --> 00:27:17.400
No doubt creating
numerous paradoxes.

00:27:17.469 --> 00:27:21.235
And who do you think
had to repair the damage? Me.

00:27:21.306 --> 00:27:23.570
She's reckless;
she has no regard

00:27:23.642 --> 00:27:25.576
for the integrity
of the timeline.

00:27:25.644 --> 00:27:26.838
I asked for her help once.

00:27:26.911 --> 00:27:28.811
She refused,
and I ended up stranded

00:27:28.880 --> 00:27:30.245
in the late 20th century.

00:27:30.315 --> 00:27:32.374
Have you ever been
to that time frame?

00:27:32.450 --> 00:27:34.384
No.

00:27:34.452 --> 00:27:36.010
Well, I don't recommend it.

00:27:36.087 --> 00:27:39.420
After three decades with those
post-industrial barbarians,

00:27:39.491 --> 00:27:42.051
I had to go through
extensive rehabilitation

00:27:42.127 --> 00:27:43.890
before I could return to duty.

00:27:43.962 --> 00:27:45.554
Avoid contact with Janeway.

00:27:45.630 --> 00:27:47.928
That's an order.

00:27:48.033 --> 00:27:50.399
Yes... sir.

00:27:54.639 --> 00:27:58.166
This will occlude
your Borg implants.

00:27:58.243 --> 00:27:59.335
Ready?

00:27:59.411 --> 00:28:00.537
Yes.

00:28:00.612 --> 00:28:02.705
We have a saying
in our line of work:

00:28:02.781 --> 00:28:04.715
"There's no time like the past."

00:28:04.783 --> 00:28:05.977
Raise shields.

00:28:06.051 --> 00:28:10.818
Time frame... Stardate
49123.5621. Delta Quadrant.

00:28:10.889 --> 00:28:15.553
Spatial coordinates...
21 Alpha Prime by 936 Zeta.

00:28:15.627 --> 00:28:19.119
Target... USS Voyager.

00:28:21.399 --> 00:28:22.889
All hands to battle stations.

00:28:23.034 --> 00:28:24.126
We're under attack.

00:28:24.202 --> 00:28:26.193
Repeat:
All hands to battle stations.

00:28:51.763 --> 00:28:53.731
Return fire.

00:28:53.798 --> 00:28:55.698
They're dropping
spatial charges.

00:28:55.767 --> 00:28:58.258
Evasive maneuvers.

00:29:00.739 --> 00:29:02.536
Shields down to 20 percent.

00:29:02.607 --> 00:29:05.007
Another Kazon ship
is approaching.

00:29:07.579 --> 00:29:09.877
Janeway to Engineering.
We need warp engines.

00:29:09.948 --> 00:29:11.210
I can't give them to you...

00:29:11.282 --> 00:29:13.512
not until I've repaired
the containment generator.

00:29:13.585 --> 00:29:14.574
Time?

00:29:14.652 --> 00:29:16.142
I'll need ten minutes, at least.

00:29:17.455 --> 00:29:20.288
Captain, I'm picking up
a strange reading on Deck 4.

00:29:20.358 --> 00:29:21.689
What kind of reading?

00:29:21.760 --> 00:29:24.593
It's a chroniton flux... .003.

00:29:27.966 --> 00:29:29.729
Any idea what's causing it?

00:29:29.801 --> 00:29:31.928
Not yet.

00:29:33.238 --> 00:29:36.833
It could be random interference
from Kazon weapons fire.

00:29:36.908 --> 00:29:37.897
I don't think so.

00:29:37.976 --> 00:29:41.673
I've seen these readings before.

00:29:57.662 --> 00:29:59.892
There's no sign of the weapon.

00:29:59.964 --> 00:30:01.591
Any uninvited guests?

00:30:02.767 --> 00:30:04.257
Not yet.

00:30:05.870 --> 00:30:08.930
The lead vessel's been disabled;
the others are regrouping.

00:30:09.007 --> 00:30:09.939
B'Elanna, status?

00:30:10.074 --> 00:30:11.371
Warp drive's on line,

00:30:11.442 --> 00:30:13.774
but the containment field's
still unstable.

00:30:13.845 --> 00:30:15.813
Warp 2 is the best
I can give you.

00:30:15.880 --> 00:30:17.211
I'll take it.

00:30:17.282 --> 00:30:19.079
Engage.

00:30:26.858 --> 00:30:28.553
They're not pursuing.

00:30:28.626 --> 00:30:30.093
Dry dock.

00:30:30.161 --> 00:30:31.458
Ma'am?

00:30:31.529 --> 00:30:34.965
The first time I saw these
readings was over two years ago

00:30:35.033 --> 00:30:36.762
when Voyager was in dry dock.

00:30:36.835 --> 00:30:38.803
Same readings, same location.

00:30:38.870 --> 00:30:39.802
What caused them?

00:30:39.871 --> 00:30:40.803
I never found out.

00:30:40.872 --> 00:30:41.839
The signal vanished

00:30:41.906 --> 00:30:43.271
before we could isolate it.

00:30:43.341 --> 00:30:45.901
Erect a level-10 force field
around that section.

00:30:45.977 --> 00:30:48.605
Is this really the time
to be chasing sensor ghosts?

00:30:48.680 --> 00:30:51.478
Something tells me
this is more than a coincidence.

00:30:51.549 --> 00:30:53.813
Seal off Deck 4.
Tuvok, you're with me.

00:30:59.924 --> 00:31:02.688
They've erected force fields
around my location.

00:31:02.760 --> 00:31:04.193
I may have been detected.

00:31:04.262 --> 00:31:05.320
How shall I proceed?

00:31:07.599 --> 00:31:08.759
Lieutenant, respond.

00:31:08.833 --> 00:31:10.061
What's wrong?

00:31:10.134 --> 00:31:12.329
The force fields are blocking
our transmissions.

00:31:12.403 --> 00:31:13.563
Compensate.

00:31:15.206 --> 00:31:16.935
Seven of Nine, report.

00:31:17.041 --> 00:31:18.406
Relativity, are you there?

00:31:18.476 --> 00:31:20.307
It's no use, sir;
she can't hear us.

00:31:32.557 --> 00:31:35.651
I don't believe
we've been introduced, Ensign.

00:31:35.727 --> 00:31:37.354
Lower the force field.

00:31:38.563 --> 00:31:39.655
I stand corrected.

00:31:39.731 --> 00:31:41.426
We have met.

00:31:41.499 --> 00:31:43.194
Utopia Planitia.

00:31:43.268 --> 00:31:44.701
The briefing room.

00:31:44.769 --> 00:31:47.169
You told me it was "efficient."

00:31:47.238 --> 00:31:47.966
Janeway...

00:31:48.106 --> 00:31:50.074
You've mistaken me
for someone else.

00:31:50.141 --> 00:31:51.699
Oh, I don't think so.

00:31:51.776 --> 00:31:54.210
So, here you are,
two years later

00:31:54.279 --> 00:31:55.769
on the other side of the galaxy.

00:31:55.847 --> 00:31:56.973
Imagine that.

00:31:57.115 --> 00:31:59.709
You are preventing me
from completing a vital mission.

00:31:59.784 --> 00:32:02.309
Who are you, and what are
you doing on my ship?

00:32:02.387 --> 00:32:03.581
Don't say anything.

00:32:03.655 --> 00:32:05.520
She can't hear you, sir.

00:32:05.590 --> 00:32:07.717
My designation is irrelevant,
but I assure you I have

00:32:07.792 --> 00:32:08.724
no hostile intentions.

00:32:08.793 --> 00:32:10.556
Somehow, I don't find that
very comforting.

00:32:10.628 --> 00:32:12.596
Are you working with the Kazon?

00:32:12.664 --> 00:32:13.631
No, I am not.

00:32:13.698 --> 00:32:15.893
I'm detecting
biomechanical implants.

00:32:15.967 --> 00:32:18.492
They have a Borg signature.

00:32:18.569 --> 00:32:20.161
Janeway to the Bridge.

00:32:20.238 --> 00:32:21.535
Scan the vicinity
for Borg ships.

00:32:21.606 --> 00:32:22.538
Did you say Borg?

00:32:22.607 --> 00:32:23.539
Do it.

00:32:23.608 --> 00:32:25.041
You will find none.

00:32:25.109 --> 00:32:26.371
Then how did you get here?

00:32:26.444 --> 00:32:28.537
I'm no longer Borg.

00:32:28.613 --> 00:32:30.205
Then who are you?

00:32:31.616 --> 00:32:33.550
I can't answer your questions.

00:32:33.618 --> 00:32:34.380
Good.

00:32:34.452 --> 00:32:35.384
Why not?

00:32:35.453 --> 00:32:36.442
It would be a violation

00:32:36.521 --> 00:32:37.954
of the Temporal Prime Directive.

00:32:38.022 --> 00:32:39.580
You're from another time?

00:32:39.657 --> 00:32:41.522
Yes.

00:32:41.592 --> 00:32:42.422
No...

00:32:42.493 --> 00:32:44.051
Who sent you?

00:32:44.128 --> 00:32:45.117
I can't tell you that.

00:32:45.196 --> 00:32:47.187
I would be risking damage
to the timeline.

00:32:47.265 --> 00:32:49.062
I don't care if history itself
comes unraveled.

00:32:49.133 --> 00:32:51.101
I want to know
why you're on my ship.

00:32:53.938 --> 00:32:55.269
What's that?

00:32:55.340 --> 00:32:57.274
You must release me.

00:32:57.342 --> 00:32:58.775
Why?

00:32:58.843 --> 00:33:01.641
Voyager is in grave danger.

00:33:01.713 --> 00:33:03.078
So we've noticed.

00:33:03.147 --> 00:33:05.172
Not from the Kazon,
from an act of sabotage.

00:33:05.249 --> 00:33:07.615
I've been sent here to stop it.

00:33:07.685 --> 00:33:09.550
The intruder has already
boarded the ship.

00:33:09.620 --> 00:33:11.918
Please, your lives depend on it.

00:33:12.023 --> 00:33:14.924
You're not going anywhere until
you tell me what's happening.

00:33:15.994 --> 00:33:16.926
My name is Seven of Nine.

00:33:16.995 --> 00:33:18.758
I'm a member of your crew...

00:33:18.830 --> 00:33:21.628
rather, I will be
a member of your crew.

00:33:21.699 --> 00:33:23.929
I've traveled back in time
to try to prevent a disaster

00:33:24.035 --> 00:33:25.093
that will destroy Voyager.

00:33:25.169 --> 00:33:26.101
Get her out of there.

00:33:26.170 --> 00:33:27.137
I'm trying.

00:33:28.373 --> 00:33:30.364
Let's see if I've got
this straight.

00:33:30.441 --> 00:33:34.468
You're a Borg drone attempting
to prevent a disaster

00:33:34.545 --> 00:33:37.105
that won't occur
for another three years.

00:33:37.181 --> 00:33:39.649
Three years, six months,
and two days.

00:33:40.718 --> 00:33:42.549
Does this make any sense to you?

00:33:42.620 --> 00:33:44.952
Like most time paradoxes,
it's implausible,

00:33:45.023 --> 00:33:47.321
but not necessarily illogical.

00:33:47.392 --> 00:33:49.121
Captain...

00:33:49.193 --> 00:33:52.321
when you take me from the Borg,
you are going to tell me

00:33:52.397 --> 00:33:55.195
that part of being human
is learning to trust.

00:33:55.266 --> 00:33:58.201
Trust me. Now.

00:34:05.943 --> 00:34:07.877
Lower the force field.

00:34:13.084 --> 00:34:15.609
Seven of Nine to Braxton.
Respond.

00:34:15.686 --> 00:34:17.620
Stay where you are.
We're pulling you out.

00:34:17.688 --> 00:34:20.122
That would be unwise.
I am pursuing the saboteur...

00:34:20.191 --> 00:34:22.125
with Captain Janeway's
assistance.

00:34:24.429 --> 00:34:26.454
Tempus fugit.

00:34:28.699 --> 00:34:30.564
Proceed.

00:34:30.635 --> 00:34:31.727
Yes, sir.

00:34:33.204 --> 00:34:35.434
The intruder is
in Junction 52 Beta.

00:34:35.506 --> 00:34:37.030
Take the starboard hatch.

00:34:37.108 --> 00:34:38.871
Aye, Captain.

00:34:45.550 --> 00:34:47.279
Captain Braxton...

00:34:56.994 --> 00:34:58.359
Lower the temporal disruptor.

00:34:59.864 --> 00:35:01.195
It's armed.

00:35:01.265 --> 00:35:02.994
I'll activate it.

00:35:03.067 --> 00:35:05.035
Lower your weapons.

00:35:09.107 --> 00:35:10.506
Janeway...

00:35:10.575 --> 00:35:12.509
Have we met?

00:35:12.577 --> 00:35:14.841
Too many times,
but you wouldn't remember.

00:35:14.912 --> 00:35:16.277
They haven't occurred yet.

00:35:16.347 --> 00:35:17.905
Seven of Nine, report.

00:35:18.015 --> 00:35:20.108
I have located the saboteur.

00:35:20.184 --> 00:35:21.310
Who is it?

00:35:21.385 --> 00:35:23.876
It's you, Captain Braxton.

00:35:23.955 --> 00:35:25.013
Me?

00:35:25.089 --> 00:35:26.454
More accurately, a future you.

00:35:26.524 --> 00:35:28.890
Now, let me complete
our mission.

00:35:28.960 --> 00:35:32.418
Our mission? I don't know
what you're talking about.

00:35:32.497 --> 00:35:33.555
Listen...

00:35:33.631 --> 00:35:34.928
very carefully.

00:35:35.066 --> 00:35:37.034
The circumstances of your life

00:35:37.101 --> 00:35:39.092
are going to change
in the next few years.

00:35:39.170 --> 00:35:41.263
You'll be sent
into rehabilitation again,

00:35:41.339 --> 00:35:42.567
forced to retire.

00:35:42.640 --> 00:35:44.733
And it's all because of Voyager.

00:35:44.809 --> 00:35:47.073
Captain, I believe
your future self

00:35:47.145 --> 00:35:49.613
is suffering
from temporal psychosis.

00:35:49.680 --> 00:35:51.375
Well, of course, I am,
you pedantic drone.

00:35:51.449 --> 00:35:54.816
The only way for me...
for us to recover

00:35:54.886 --> 00:35:57.184
is to obliterate Voyager
from the timeline.

00:35:57.255 --> 00:35:59.951
That way, none of the events
that caused this illness

00:36:00.024 --> 00:36:01.116
will have occurred.

00:36:01.192 --> 00:36:02.386
What events?

00:36:02.460 --> 00:36:05.759
30 years of exile
on 20th century Earth,

00:36:05.830 --> 00:36:08.890
the temporal inversion
in the Takara Sector,

00:36:09.000 --> 00:36:12.458
three violations
that I had to repair.

00:36:12.537 --> 00:36:14.562
Can you get a lock on him?

00:36:14.639 --> 00:36:17.335
Negative. He's activated
a dispersal node.

00:36:17.408 --> 00:36:20.172
I should say... you've activated

00:36:20.244 --> 00:36:21.233
a dispersal node.

00:36:21.312 --> 00:36:22.472
Don't be absurd.

00:36:22.547 --> 00:36:24.742
I have no wish
to sabotage Voyager.

00:36:24.815 --> 00:36:26.339
Not yet.

00:36:26.417 --> 00:36:28.282
Remodulate the transporters.

00:36:28.352 --> 00:36:31.515
Find a way to cut
through the interference.

00:36:32.757 --> 00:36:34.657
I gave you an order, Lieutenant.

00:36:34.725 --> 00:36:36.818
I'm sorry, sir.

00:36:36.894 --> 00:36:38.919
I'm taking command
of this vessel...

00:36:38.996 --> 00:36:40.691
and I'm relieving you of duty

00:36:40.765 --> 00:36:43.632
for crimes...
you're going to commit.

00:36:43.701 --> 00:36:45.430
I haven't done anything.

00:36:46.504 --> 00:36:48.335
Seven of Nine...

00:36:48.406 --> 00:36:49.771
apprehend Braxton.

00:36:53.344 --> 00:36:54.834
No.

00:36:58.916 --> 00:37:00.781
Relativity, he's escaped.

00:37:00.851 --> 00:37:01.943
I'm tracking him.

00:37:02.019 --> 00:37:04.385
He's traveled
to another time frame...

00:37:04.455 --> 00:37:05.820
two years earlier.

00:37:05.890 --> 00:37:07.790
Transport me
to those coordinates.

00:37:07.858 --> 00:37:09.689
That would be your fourth jump.

00:37:09.760 --> 00:37:12.228
I am aware of the risks.

00:37:12.296 --> 00:37:14.560
Stand by.

00:37:14.632 --> 00:37:17.328
Thank you for your assistance.

00:37:39.156 --> 00:37:40.919
There's still
some work to be done,

00:37:41.025 --> 00:37:42.754
but, uh, once
the sawdust clears,

00:37:42.827 --> 00:37:44.294
I think you'll be impressed.

00:37:44.362 --> 00:37:47.354
Voyager may not be as big
as a Galaxy-class ship,

00:37:47.431 --> 00:37:48.864
but she's...

00:37:50.935 --> 00:37:52.368
Take cover!

00:37:56.240 --> 00:37:58.868
Security, report
to Deck 4, Section 12.

00:37:58.943 --> 00:38:01.776
Erect force fields around
all access points.

00:38:02.947 --> 00:38:05.074
Is this part of the tour?

00:38:28.706 --> 00:38:30.105
I've lost him.

00:38:30.174 --> 00:38:32.699
He's still on Voyager,
but he's gone five years ahead.

00:38:34.812 --> 00:38:36.575
Initiate transport.

00:38:52.863 --> 00:38:54.160
Point, server.

00:38:54.231 --> 00:38:56.495
It's all in the wrist.

00:38:56.567 --> 00:38:57.932
Score?

00:38:58.035 --> 00:38:59.935
19-18.

00:39:02.173 --> 00:39:03.572
Who are you?

00:39:08.579 --> 00:39:10.945
Bridge, intruder alert,
Deck 2.

00:39:25.930 --> 00:39:27.022
Explain.

00:39:27.098 --> 00:39:29.089
No time.
You must apprehend him.

00:39:29.166 --> 00:39:31.191
He's trying to destroy Voyager.

00:39:31.268 --> 00:39:32.496
Seven of Nine, status.

00:39:32.570 --> 00:39:35.232
I am incapacitated...
it's sensory aphasia.

00:39:35.306 --> 00:39:36.364
Stand by.

00:39:36.440 --> 00:39:38.142
I'm pulling you out.

00:39:38.209 --> 00:39:39.471
Stop him.

00:39:39.543 --> 00:39:41.477
Your future depends on it.

00:39:53.457 --> 00:39:55.118
Braxton?

00:39:55.192 --> 00:39:56.819
I disabled his tricorder.

00:39:56.894 --> 00:39:58.054
He's trapped there.

00:39:58.129 --> 00:40:00.188
Seven of Nine is pursuing him.

00:40:00.264 --> 00:40:01.526
She is efficient.

00:40:01.599 --> 00:40:03.191
She will succeed.

00:40:03.267 --> 00:40:04.632
Let's hope so...

00:40:04.702 --> 00:40:06.932
because we've
run out of options.

00:40:17.181 --> 00:40:18.773
You again.

00:40:18.849 --> 00:40:21.340
I don't believe we've met,
Ensign.

00:40:23.721 --> 00:40:25.211
No, I'm wrong.

00:40:25.289 --> 00:40:27.917
We have met.

00:40:27.992 --> 00:40:29.823
Captain Braxton.

00:40:29.894 --> 00:40:31.259
Not anymore.

00:40:31.328 --> 00:40:33.956
I've lost my rank,
thanks to you.

00:40:34.098 --> 00:40:36.828
Seven of Nine to Seven of Nine.

00:40:36.901 --> 00:40:37.925
What's your status?

00:40:38.002 --> 00:40:39.435
We've apprehended Braxton.

00:40:39.503 --> 00:40:40.868
How shall we proceed?

00:40:40.938 --> 00:40:42.371
Stand by.

00:40:54.518 --> 00:40:57.214
Long time no see.

00:41:01.926 --> 00:41:03.518
Are you all right, Seven?

00:41:03.594 --> 00:41:07.462
I believe we've just prevented
Voyager's destruction.

00:41:07.531 --> 00:41:09.897
Would you care
to explain how you...

00:41:25.015 --> 00:41:27.745
The Timeship Relativity.

00:41:27.818 --> 00:41:29.080
We need your help.

00:41:29.153 --> 00:41:30.916
This Seven of Nine
stopped Braxton,

00:41:30.988 --> 00:41:32.216
but she created

00:41:32.289 --> 00:41:34.416
several temporal incursions
along the way.

00:41:34.492 --> 00:41:36.960
She instigated a phaser fight
at Utopia Planetia;

00:41:37.061 --> 00:41:39.120
she was seen by you
and Lieutenant Tuvok

00:41:39.196 --> 00:41:41.130
two years before
she joined your crew;

00:41:41.198 --> 00:41:43.223
and she interacted
with her past self

00:41:43.300 --> 00:41:46.326
in front of 15 crew members
at a Ping-Pong tournament

00:41:46.403 --> 00:41:50.339
approximately six minutes ago...
your time frame, of course.

00:41:50.407 --> 00:41:52.068
Of course.

00:41:52.142 --> 00:41:54.440
Needless to say, we need
to clean up the timeline.

00:41:54.512 --> 00:41:56.139
Someone must go back
to the beginning

00:41:56.213 --> 00:41:58.306
and prevent the chain of events
from occurring

00:41:58.382 --> 00:41:59.747
in the first place.

00:41:59.817 --> 00:42:02.843
I can't make another jump
without damaging myself.

00:42:04.722 --> 00:42:07.452
I get the feeling
I'm about to be drafted.

00:42:07.525 --> 00:42:10.153
In exchange for leniency,
Captain Braxton informs us

00:42:10.227 --> 00:42:12.252
of the precise moment
he boarded Voyager

00:42:12.329 --> 00:42:13.728
to plant the weapon.

00:42:13.797 --> 00:42:15.389
We'll be sending you
to stop him.

00:42:15.466 --> 00:42:16.433
Tell her.

00:42:16.500 --> 00:42:18.730
Deck 4, Section 38.

00:42:18.802 --> 00:42:21.100
I'll stumble over
a wounded crew member.

00:42:21.171 --> 00:42:23.469
That will be your chance
to capture me.

00:42:23.541 --> 00:42:26.806
Don't miss it, or we'll have
to do this all over again.

00:42:26.877 --> 00:42:29.141
Wait a minute,
let me get this straight.

00:42:29.213 --> 00:42:32.114
I'm going back in time
to stop Braxton...

00:42:33.751 --> 00:42:35.844
But you already have him.

00:42:35.920 --> 00:42:37.683
And there's a third one
in our brig.

00:42:37.755 --> 00:42:39.245
I arrested him earlier today.

00:42:39.323 --> 00:42:40.290
But don't worry.

00:42:40.357 --> 00:42:41.949
They'll all be reintegrated

00:42:42.059 --> 00:42:43.822
in time for the trial.

00:42:47.064 --> 00:42:48.122
And Seven?

00:42:48.198 --> 00:42:50.826
Oh, I assure you
when all this is over,

00:42:50.901 --> 00:42:52.835
there'll be just one
Seven of Nine.

00:42:52.903 --> 00:42:54.461
All right.
Let's get started

00:42:54.538 --> 00:42:56.369
before my headache
gets any worse.

00:43:03.681 --> 00:43:05.376
Captain, a Kazon torpedo

00:43:05.449 --> 00:43:07.644
just blew out
the containment generator.

00:43:07.718 --> 00:43:09.913
Do you want me
to reroute emergency power

00:43:10.020 --> 00:43:11.715
or take the warp core off-line?

00:43:11.789 --> 00:43:13.086
Use your best judgment.

00:43:13.157 --> 00:43:15.125
I thought you were on
your way to the Bridge.

00:43:15.192 --> 00:43:16.921
I have to take care
of something first.

00:43:16.994 --> 00:43:19.189
Now, get moving, Lieutenant.

00:43:31.342 --> 00:43:34.607
Send damage control teams
to Decks 9 through 14.

00:43:34.678 --> 00:43:36.270
Seal the breaches if you can.

00:43:36.347 --> 00:43:37.541
I'll be on the Bridge.

00:43:37.615 --> 00:43:38.639
Keep me informed.

00:43:38.716 --> 00:43:39.910
Yes, ma'am.

00:43:55.666 --> 00:43:57.463
Come here often?

00:44:07.011 --> 00:44:10.879
Incursion factor... .0036.

00:44:10.948 --> 00:44:13.178
That's better than I expected.

00:44:13.250 --> 00:44:15.309
Glad we could lend a hand.

00:44:16.654 --> 00:44:17.916
When do we go home?

00:44:17.988 --> 00:44:20.252
You'll both be returned
to your time frame.

00:44:20.324 --> 00:44:23.088
You'll be reintegrated
with the other Seven of Nine.

00:44:23.160 --> 00:44:24.627
Since none of your time-jumps

00:44:24.695 --> 00:44:27.289
were to your foreseeable
future... only the past...

00:44:27.364 --> 00:44:29.924
I see no reason to resequence
your memory engrams.

00:44:30.034 --> 00:44:32.264
But remember the Temporal
Prime Directive.

00:44:32.336 --> 00:44:34.304
Discuss your experiences
with no one.

00:44:34.371 --> 00:44:36.168
Understood.

00:44:39.743 --> 00:44:41.506
Oh, Captain...

00:44:41.578 --> 00:44:43.512
Braxton was right
about one thing...

00:44:43.580 --> 00:44:46.549
Voyager shows up on our sensors
far too often.

00:44:46.617 --> 00:44:49.245
Try to avoid time travel.

00:44:50.788 --> 00:44:52.813
See you in the 24th century.

00:44:52.890 --> 00:44:54.824
I look forward to it.

00:44:54.892 --> 00:44:56.689
Or should I say backward?

00:44:56.760 --> 00:44:58.728
Don't get started.
